{"id":"n5-049","title":"Verb て ください (Verb-te kudasai)","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"A request or command; 'please do'.","longExplanation":"The て ください grammar point is used to make a request or command someone to do something politely. The verb is conjugated into its て-form and followed by ください, which means 'please'. This structure is used when asking someone to do something with a polite and respectful tone.","formation":"Verb-て form + ください","examples":[{"jp":"ドアを開けてください。","romaji":"Doa wo akete kudasai.","en":"Please open the door.","words":[{"surface":"ドア","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"開け","vocabId":"1202450","reading":"あける"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"電話番号を教えてください。","romaji":"Denwa bangou wo oshiete kudasai.","en":"Please tell me your phone number.","words":[{"surface":"電話","vocabId":"1443840","reading":"でんわ"},{"surface":"番号","vocabId":"1482290","reading":"ばんごう"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"教え","vocabId":"1236890","reading":"おしえ"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"ゆっくり話してください。","romaji":"Yukkuri hanashite kudasai.","en":"Please speak slowly.","words":[{"surface":"ゆっくり","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話し","vocabId":"1562350","reading":"はなす"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"コーヒーを一つ持ってきてください。","romaji":"Koohii wo hitotsu motte kite kudasai.","en":"Please bring me a coffee.","words":[{"surface":"コーヒー","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"一つ","vocabId":"1160820","reading":"ひとつ"},{"surface":"持っ","vocabId":"1315720","reading":"もつ"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"き","vocabId":"1221520","reading":"き"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]}]}